  "liner": {
   "body_md": "This audience recording captures the Mountain Goats performing on Saturday, December 6, 1997, at The Empty Bottle in Chicago, Illinois [1]. The eighty-minute set includes twenty songs, offering a comprehensive look at the band's lineup from that period [1]. Several tracks are notably rare, with only a handful of archived performances available elsewhere [1]. The setlist features the first archived appearances of \"There Will Be No Divorce\" and \"Love Cuts the Strings\" [1]. Additionally, the performance of \"Reel Around the Fountain\" is the only archived rendition of that song in the collection [1]. This recording is the sole available capture of the show, rated five out of five by one listener [1]. A review of this specific recording notes that the audio quality is well-suited to the era and that the song selection is nearly perfect [2]. The reviewer highlighted the return of banter and identified \"The Sign\" as the best played song [2]. They also noted that \"There Will Be No Divorce\" was a standout, ranking it among their top favorites from that time [2]. This show is the seventeenth of four hundred and sixty-seven archived performances by the Mountain Goats [3]. The previous archived show was recorded on July 16, 1997, at the Capitol Theater [3].",
